-- GOSAIKUNDA LAKE TREK (Langtang)
('Gosaikunda Lake Trek','gosaikunda-lake-trek','A sacred alpine lake trek through Langtang National Park with stunning Himalayan views and rich Hindu-Buddhist mythology.','The Gosaikunda Lake trek is within Langtang National Park and takes in the high-altitude freshwater lake of Gosaikunda (4,380m). Gosaikunda is not only a Ramsar site (since 2007), meaning that it is a wetland of international importance, but it is also a site considered holy to Buddhists and Hindus. On this week-long trek, you will have dramatic views of the Manaslu range, Ganesh Himal range, Tibetan peaks, and Langtang Lirung, as well as the three lakes of Gosaikunda, Saraswati Kunda, and Bhairab Kunda. In Hindu mythology, Gosaikunda is the abode of the gods Shiva and Gauri. It is believed that Lord Shiva formed the lake when he thrust his holy trident into the mountain to extract water to drink. The waters are considered significant during the Janai Purnima festival at the full moon in August when thousands of pilgrims gather.','https://images.pexels.com/photos/2387873/pexels-photo-2387873.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1600','8 Days','Moderate','$850','Trek',20,
'[{"day":1,"title":"Kathmandu to Syabrubesi (Drive)","description":"7-8 hour scenic drive from Kathmandu to Syabrubesi (1,550m) through the Trisuli Valley. Overnight in teahouse."},{"day":2,"title":"Trek to Lama Hotel","description":"6-7 hour trek through lush bamboo and rhododendron forests alongside the Langtang River to Lama Hotel (2,380m)."},{"day":3,"title":"Lama Hotel to Thulo Syabru","description":"5-6 hour trek through dense forests with rhododendrons and oak trees, passing landslide areas and the charming village of Bamboo."},{"day":4,"title":"Thulo Syabru to Shin Gompa","description":"3-4 hour trek with steep ascent from Thulo Syabru (2,330m) through open landscapes to Shin Gompa (3,330m). Visit the local cheese factory."},{"day":5,"title":"Shin Gompa to Gosaikunda","description":"5-6 hour challenging ascent to Gosaikunda (4,460m). Cross Lauribina La Pass (4,610m). Reach the sacred glacial lakes."},{"day":6,"title":"Gosaikunda to Chandanbari","description":"6-7 hour mainly downhill trek retracing steps through Langtang Valley to Chandanbari (2,000m)."},{"day":7,"title":"Chandanbari to Dhunche","description":"8 hour descent through rhododendron and pine forests to Dhunche (1,300m)."},{"day":8,"title":"Dhunche to Kathmandu (Drive)","description":"6-8 hour drive back to Kathmandu (1,380m)."}]'::jsonb,
'["7 nights teahouse accommodation","Guide for 8 days","Kathmandu-Syabrubesi-Kathmandu local bus","Langtang National Park permit","8 breakfasts, 8 lunches, 7 dinners on trek"]'::jsonb,
'["Porter (optional USD 184)","Private Jeep (optional USD 260)","Hot/cold drinks","Travel insurance","Personal expenses","Tips"]'::jsonb,
'["Sacred Gosaikunda Lake — holy alpine lake revered by Hindus and Buddhists","Stunning views of Langtang, Ganesh Himal, and Manaslu ranges","Diverse landscapes from lush forests to glacial lakes","Rich Tamang and Sherpa culture","Cross Lauribina Pass (4,610m)","Janai Purnima festival pilgrimage in August"]'::jsonb),

-- TAMANG HERITAGE TREK (Langtang)
('Tamang Heritage Trek','tamang-heritage-trek','A cultural trek through traditional Tamang villages with stunning mountain views and authentic homestay experiences.','The Tamang Heritage Trek starts by driving from Kathmandu to Syafru Beshi and runs through the beautiful Langtang Valley with breathtaking views of Langtang and Ganesh Himal. Villages on the route are occupied by Tamang people, closely related to Tibetans, and so the culture is Buddhist with a good scattering of prayer wheels, chortens, prayer flags, and mani stones along the trails. The Tamang Heritage Trail lies in what was previously a restricted area near the Tibet border and was opened up to visitors lately. The people in this area have a culture, tradition, and religion that goes back hundreds of years, and the craftsmanship, dress, and stone-mud houses are testimony of this ancient background. For those interested in anthropology as well as trekking, this is the perfect trip.','https://images.pexels.com/photos/2387871/pexels-photo-2387871.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1600','11 Days','Moderate','$1,050','Trek',21,
'[{"day":1,"title":"Kathmandu to Syabrubesi (Drive)","description":"7-8 hour drive to Syabrubesi (1,460m). Overnight in teahouse."},{"day":2,"title":"Syabrubesi to Gatlang","description":"5 hour trek through yak pastures, lush forests, and rivers. Views of Ganesh Himal. Overnight Gatlang (2,238m)."},{"day":3,"title":"Gatlang to Tatopani","description":"6-7 hour trek descending through forests to Chilime, crossing Chilime Hydropower Dam. Overnight Tatopani (2,600m)."},{"day":4,"title":"Tatopani to Thuman","description":"5-6 hour trek through forests and cultivated land with mani walls. Traditional stone and wood Tamang architecture. Overnight Thuman (2,340m)."},{"day":5,"title":"Thuman to Briddim (via Lingling Pass)","description":"5-6 hour trek descending through forests, crossing Bhote Koshi River. Overnight Briddim (2,500m) with authentic homestay."},{"day":6,"title":"Briddim to Lama Hotel","description":"5-6 hour trek descending through forests with birdlife, crossing Ghopche Khola. Overnight Lama Hotel (2,480m)."},{"day":7,"title":"Lama Hotel to Langtang Village","description":"6-7 hour trek with 1,000m altitude gain. Pass Ghoretable. Views of Langtang range. Overnight Langtang Village (3,430m)."},{"day":8,"title":"Langtang Village to Kyanjin Gompa","description":"4 hour gradual climb upstream of Langtang River. Visit Kyanjin Gompa monastery. Overnight Kyanjin Gompa (3,870m)."},{"day":9,"title":"Kyanjin Gompa to Lama Hotel","description":"6 hour descent retracing steps through Mundu, Ghora Tabela. Overnight Lama Hotel."},{"day":10,"title":"Lama Hotel to Syabrubesi","description":"4 hour last hiking day along Langtang River. Overnight Syabrubesi."},{"day":11,"title":"Syabrubesi to Kathmandu (Drive)","description":"8-9 hour drive back to Kathmandu."}]'::jsonb,
'["10 nights teahouse accommodation","Guide for 11 days","Kathmandu-Syabrubesi-Kathmandu local bus","Langtang National Park permit","11 breakfasts, 10 lunches, 10 dinners on trek"]'::jsonb,
'["Porter (optional USD 230)","Private Jeep (optional USD 260)","Hotel in Kathmandu","Hot/cold drinks","Travel insurance","Personal expenses","Tips"]'::jsonb,
'["Rich Tamang culture and traditions","Traditional Tibetan-style houses and architecture","Views of Langtang, Ganesh Himal, and Tibetan peaks","Natural hot springs at Tatopani","Ancient monasteries and Buddhist prayer wheels","Authentic homestay in Briddim village"]'::jsonb),

-- HELAMBU TREK (Langtang)
('Helambu Trek','helambu-trek','A peaceful trek through Hyolmo villages and rhododendron forests, close to Kathmandu with stunning Himalayan views.','The Helambu Trek is a beautiful and accessible trek just north of Kathmandu, offering a perfect short adventure for those with limited time. The trail passes through picturesque Hyolmo (Sherpa) villages, lush rhododendron and pine forests, and offers stunning views of the Langtang range, Ganesh Himal, and Dorje Lakpa. Unlike the busier trekking routes, Helambu remains relatively quiet and offers an authentic cultural experience with the Hyolmo people, who share close ties with Tibetan Buddhism. The trek starts from Sundarijal at the edge of Kathmandu Valley and ends at Melamchi Bazaar.','https://images.pexels.com/photos/2901209/pexels-photo-2901209.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1600','6 Days','Moderate','$795','Trek',22,
'[{"day":1,"title":"Kathmandu to Sundarijal to Chisapani","description":"1 hour drive to Sundarijal. 4 hour trek to Chisapani (2,300m). Walk through Shivapuri National Park."},{"day":2,"title":"Chisapani to Kutumsang","description":"7 hour trek through forests and Hyolmo villages to Kutumsang (2,446m)."},{"day":3,"title":"Kutumsang to Thadepati","description":"6 hour trek to Thadepati (3,650m) — the highest point. Panoramic mountain views."},{"day":4,"title":"Thadepati to Tarke Ghyang","description":"6 hour trek descending to Tarke Ghyang (2,560m). Explore the ancient monastery."},{"day":5,"title":"Tarke Ghyang to Sermathang","description":"3-4 hour trek to Sermathang (2,610m). Beautiful Hyolmo village."},{"day":6,"title":"Sermathang to Melamchi Bazaar to Kathmandu","description":"3-4 hour trek to Melamchi. Drive back to Kathmandu."}]'::jsonb,
'["5 nights teahouse accommodation","Guide for 6 days","Kathmandu-Sundarijal & Melamchi-Kathmandu local bus","Shivapuri National Park Permit","6 breakfasts, 6 lunches, 5 dinners on trek"]'::jsonb,
'["Porter (optional USD 128)","Private Jeep (optional USD 196)","Hotel in Kathmandu","Hot/cold drinks","Travel insurance","Personal expenses","Tips"]'::jsonb,
'["Explore unique Hyolmo culture and traditional villages","Walk through lush rhododendron and pine forests","Stunning views of Langtang, Ganesh Himal, Dorje Lakpa","Ancient Buddhist monasteries and prayer wheels","Less crowded — peaceful trekking experience","Close to Kathmandu — minimal travel time"]'::jsonb),

-- ANNAPURNA BASE CAMP TREK (Annapurna)
('Annapurna Base Camp Trek','annapurna-base-camp','A spectacular trek into the heart of the Annapurna Sanctuary with 360-degree mountain views and Gurung hospitality.','The Annapurna Base Camp Trek is one of Nepal''s most beloved treks, taking you deep into the Annapurna Sanctuary — a natural amphitheater surrounded by towering peaks. At 4,130m, ABC offers a 360-degree panorama of Annapurna I (8,091m), Machhapuchhre (Fishtail), Hiunchuli, and Annapurna South. The journey passes through rhododendron forests, traditional Gurung villages, and alongside the Modi Khola River. You''ll experience two base camps — Annapurna Base Camp and Machhapuchhre Base Camp — making this an incredible value trek. The natural hot springs at Jhinu Danda provide the perfect end to the adventure.','https://images.pexels.com/photos/2356045/pexels-photo-2356045.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1600','10 Days','Moderate','$786','Trek',23,
'[{"day":1,"title":"Kathmandu to Pokhara to Ghandruk","description":"6-8 hour drive to Pokhara then 3 hour drive to Ghandruk (2,012m). Explore the beautiful Gurung village."},{"day":2,"title":"Ghandruk to Chomrong","description":"6 hour trek through terraced fields and forests with views of Machhapuchhre. Overnight Chomrong (2,170m)."},{"day":3,"title":"Chomrong to Bamboo","description":"4-5 hour trek descending to Chomrong Khola, then climbing through rhododendron and bamboo forests. Overnight Bamboo (2,310m)."},{"day":4,"title":"Bamboo to Deurali","description":"3-4 hour gentle climb through forests, passing Dovan and Himalaya. Overnight Deurali (3,230m)."},{"day":5,"title":"Deurali to Annapurna Base Camp","description":"5-6 hour trek passing Machhapuchhre Base Camp (3,700m). Enter the Annapurna Sanctuary. Reach ABC (4,130m)."},{"day":6,"title":"ABC to Bamboo","description":"6-7 hour descent retracing steps through the sanctuary. Overnight Bamboo."},{"day":7,"title":"Bamboo to Jhinu Danda","description":"5-6 hour trek with natural hot springs at Jhinu Danda (1,780m). Relax in the thermal pools beside the Modi Khola."},{"day":8,"title":"Jhinu Danda to Naya Pul to Pokhara","description":"5 hour final trek to Naya Pul. 1 hour drive to Pokhara. Celebration by Phewa Lake."},{"day":9,"title":"Pokhara to Kathmandu (Drive)","description":"7 hour drive back to Kathmandu."},{"day":10,"title":"Departure","description":"Airport transfer. End of service."}]'::jsonb,
'["7 nights teahouse accommodation","1 night Pokhara hotel","Guide for 9 days","Kathmandu-Pokhara-Kathmandu tourist bus","Pokhara-Naya Pul-Pokhara private car","ACAP permit + TIMS card","8 breakfasts, 8 lunches, 7 dinners on trek"]'::jsonb,
'["Porter (optional USD 249)","Lunch/dinner in Pokhara","Hotel in Kathmandu","Hot/cold drinks","Travel insurance","Tips"]'::jsonb,
'["360-degree mountain views at Annapurna Base Camp","Two base camps in one trek (ABC + Machhapuchhre BC)","Natural hot springs at Jhinu Danda","Gurung culture in Ghandruk village","Rhododendron forests in spring","Views of Machhapuchhre (Fishtail) mountain"]'::jsonb),

-- MARDI HIMAL BASE CAMP TREK (Annapurna)
('Mardi Himal Base Camp Trek','mardi-himal-base-camp','An off-the-beaten-path trek to the lap of Mardi Himal with stunning close-up views of Machhapuchhre.','The Mardi Himal Base Camp Trek is one of the Annapurna region''s best-kept secrets. This relatively new trekking route takes you through quiet forests, traditional villages, and alpine meadows to the base of Mardi Himal (4,450m). The trek offers incredibly close-up views of Machhapuchhre (Fishtail), Annapurna South, Hiunchuli, and the entire Annapurna massif. Unlike the busier ABC trek, Mardi Himal sees far fewer trekkers, offering a sense of solitude and pristine nature. The trail passes through rhododendron, pine, and oak forests, with the landscape transforming from lush green to stark alpine as you gain altitude.','https://images.pexels.com/photos/2901209/pexels-photo-2901209.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1600','7 Days','Moderate','$700','Trek',24,
'[{"day":1,"title":"Kathmandu to Pokhara","description":"8 hour drive or 25 minute flight to Pokhara (830m). Overnight in Pokhara."},{"day":2,"title":"Pokhara to Kande to Deurali","description":"1 hour drive to Kande. 5-6 hour trek to Deurali (2,200m)."},{"day":3,"title":"Deurali to Low Camp","description":"5-6 hour trek through rhododendron forests to Low Camp (2,900m)."},{"day":4,"title":"Low Camp to High Camp","description":"6-7 hour trek above the treeline with expanding mountain views. Overnight High Camp (3,585m)."},{"day":5,"title":"High Camp to Mardi Himal BC to Badal Danda","description":"Early start to Mardi Himal Base Camp (4,450m). Descend to Badal Danda (3,210m). 7-8 hours total."},{"day":6,"title":"Badal Danda to Sidhing to Pokhara","description":"5-6 hour trek to Sidhing. Drive back to Pokhara. Celebration evening."},{"day":7,"title":"Pokhara to Kathmandu","description":"5-7 hour drive back to Kathmandu."}]'::jsonb,
'["4 nights teahouse accommodation","1 night Pokhara hotel","Guide for 6 days","Kathmandu-Pokhara tourist bus","Pokhara-Phedi & Lwang-Pokhara private car","ACAP permit + TIMS card","6 breakfasts, 5 lunches, 5 dinners on trek"]'::jsonb,
'["Porter (optional USD 132)","Lunch/dinner in Pokhara","Hotel in Kathmandu","Hot/cold drinks","Travel insurance","Tips"]'::jsonb,
'["Off-the-beaten-path trail with fewer crowds","Close-up views of Machhapuchhre and Mardi Himal","Lush rhododendron, pine, and oak forests","Alpine meadows and pristine nature","Sense of solitude and wilderness","Stunning panoramic Himalayan views"]'::jsonb),

-- GOKYO LAKE TREK (Everest)
('Gokyo Lake Trek','gokyo-lake-trek','A stunning trek through the Everest region to the turquoise Gokyo Lakes with panoramic views from Gokyo Ri.','The Gokyo Lake Trek offers a quieter alternative to the Everest Base Camp trek with equally stunning scenery. The trek takes you to the beautiful turquoise Gokyo Lakes, a series of six glacial lakes designated as a Ramsar site. From the summit of Gokyo Ri (5,357m), you get one of the finest panoramic views in the entire Khumbu region — Everest, Lhotse, Makalu, and Cho Oyu all visible in a single sweeping vista. The trek also takes you alongside the Ngozumpa Glacier, the largest glacier in Nepal, and through traditional Sherpa villages like Namche Bazaar and Khumjung.','https://images.pexels.com/photos/2387873/pexels-photo-2387873.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1600','12 Days','Moderate','$1,250','Trek',25,
'[{"day":1,"title":"Arrive in Kathmandu","description":"Arrival and transfer to hotel. Trek briefing."},{"day":2,"title":"Fly to Lukla, Trek to Phakding","description":"Early flight to Lukla. 3-4 hour trek to Phakding (2,651m)."},{"day":3,"title":"Phakding to Namche Bazaar","description":"5-6 hour trek through pine forests and suspension bridges to Namche Bazaar (3,438m)."},{"day":4,"title":"Acclimatization in Namche","description":"Day hike to Khumjung village and Everest View Hotel. Acclimatization and exploration."},{"day":5,"title":"Namche to Dole","description":"6 hour trek through forests to Dole (3,680m)."},{"day":6,"title":"Dole to Machhermo","description":"5-6 hour trek to Machhermo (3,870m)."},{"day":7,"title":"Machhermo to Gokyo","description":"4 hour trek to Gokyo (4,800m). Afternoon hike to Gokyo Ri (5,357m) for sunset."},{"day":8,"title":"Explore Gokyo Lakes","description":"Morning hike to 4th and 5th Gokyo Lakes. Return to Machhermo (3,870m)."},{"day":9,"title":"Machhermo to Namche","description":"8 hour descent back to Namche Bazaar."},{"day":10,"title":"Namche to Lukla","description":"8 hour final trekking day back to Lukla."},{"day":11,"title":"Fly to Kathmandu","description":"Scenic flight back to Kathmandu."},{"day":12,"title":"Departure","description":"Airport transfer."}]'::jsonb,
'["Airport transfers","Kathmandu-Lukla-Kathmandu flights","2 nights Kathmandu hotel","10 nights teahouse accommodation","Guide for 11 days, Porter for 10 days","All permits (Sagarmatha NP + local)","11 breakfasts, 10 lunches, 10 dinners on trek"]'::jsonb,
'["Lunch and dinner in Kathmandu","Hot/cold drinks","Travel insurance","Personal expenses","Tips"]'::jsonb,
'["Turquoise Gokyo Lakes — a Ramsar site","Gokyo Ri (5,357m) — panoramic Everest views","Ngozumpa Glacier — largest glacier in Nepal","Sherpa culture in Namche and Khumjung","Fewer crowds than the EBC trek","Views of Everest, Lhotse, Makalu, and Cho Oyu"]'::jsonb),

-- 7 DAYS EVEREST BASE CAMP TREK WITH HELICOPTER RETURN
('7 Days Everest Base Camp Trek with Helicopter Return','everest-base-camp-helicopter-return','A shortened EBC trek with a spectacular helicopter return — see Everest in under a week.','This 7-day Everest Base Camp trek is designed for those with limited time who still want to experience the magic of the Khumbu. You''ll trek through the classic route to Tengboche, experiencing the Sherpa culture, suspension bridges, and stunning mountain scenery. Then, instead of trekking back, you''ll board a helicopter from Tengboche that flies over Everest Base Camp and lands at Kala Patthar (5,545m) for the iconic Everest photo, before flying you directly back to Kathmandu. This is the most efficient way to experience the world''s highest mountain.','https://images.pexels.com/photos/933054/pexels-photo-933054.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1600','7 Days','Strenuous','$2,499','Trek',26,
'[{"day":1,"title":"Welcome to Kathmandu","description":"Arrival and hotel transfer. Pre-trek briefing."},{"day":2,"title":"Fly to Lukla, Trek to Phakding","description":"Early flight to Lukla. 3-4 hour trek to Phakding (2,651m)."},{"day":3,"title":"Phakding to Namche Bazaar","description":"5-6 hour trek crossing 5 suspension bridges to Namche Bazaar (3,440m)."},{"day":4,"title":"Acclimatization in Namche","description":"Day hike to Khumjung village and Everest View Hotel."},{"day":5,"title":"Namche to Tengboche","description":"5-6 hour trek to Tengboche (3,956m). Visit the famous monastery."},{"day":6,"title":"Helicopter: Tengboche to EBC to Kala Patthar to Kathmandu","description":"Helicopter flight from Tengboche over Everest Base Camp with landing at Kala Patthar (5,545m). Fly back to Kathmandu."},{"day":7,"title":"Final Departure","description":"Airport transfer. End of service."}]'::jsonb,
'["Airport transfers","Kathmandu-Lukla flight","Helicopter Tengboche-EBC-Kala Patthar-Kathmandu","5 nights teahouse accommodation","2 nights Kathmandu hotel","Guide for 7 days, Porter for 6 days","All permits","7 breakfasts, 6 lunches, 6 dinners on trek"]'::jsonb,
'["Lunch/dinner in Kathmandu","Hot/cold drinks","Travel insurance","Personal expenses","Tips","WiFi card (USD 25)"]'::jsonb,
'["Fly to Lukla — world''s most thrilling airport","Helicopter return — no long hike back","Sherpa culture in Namche Bazaar","Tengboche Monastery","Kala Patthar (5,545m) — best Everest views","Complete experience in just 7 days"]'::jsonb),

-- TSUM VALLEY TREK (Manaslu)
('Tsum Valley Trek','tsum-valley-trek','A sacred hidden valley of Tibetan Buddhism, remote monasteries, and stunning Himalayan landscapes.','The Tsum Valley Trek takes you into one of Nepal''s most spiritually significant regions. Not opened to trekkers until 2008, this remote valley is known as the "Hidden Valley" and is rich in Tibetan Buddhist culture. The trail passes through ancient monasteries including Mu Gompa and Rachen Gompa, visits Milarepa''s meditation cave, and offers stunning views of Mt. Manaslu (8,163m), the 8th highest mountain in the world. The Tsum people are of Tibetan origin, and the valley is dotted with chortens, mani walls, and prayer flags.','https://images.pexels.com/photos/1183099/pexels-photo-1183099.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1600','11 Days','Moderate','$1,100','Trek',27,
'[{"day":1,"title":"Drive Kathmandu to Machha Khola","description":"9 hour drive from Kathmandu to Machha Khola (930m)."},{"day":2,"title":"Machha Khola to Jagat","description":"6-7 hour trek through forests and along the Budhi Gandaki River."},{"day":3,"title":"Jagat to Lokpa","description":"5-6 hour trek entering the Manaslu Conservation Area."},{"day":4,"title":"Lokpa to Chumling","description":"5 hour trek entering the Tsum Valley. Traditional Tibetan villages."},{"day":5,"title":"Chumling to Chekampar","description":"3-4 hour trek with views of Ganesh Himal."},{"day":6,"title":"Chekampar to Nile","description":"3-4 hour trek passing ancient monasteries."},{"day":7,"title":"Day trip to Mu Gompa","description":"7 hour round trip hike to Mu Gompa (3,700m) — the highest monastery in the valley."},{"day":8,"title":"Return to Chumling","description":"5-6 hour descent back through the valley."},{"day":9,"title":"Chumling to Philim","description":"6-7 hour trek descending through forests."},{"day":10,"title":"Philim to Machha Khola","description":"6-7 hour trek back to the trailhead."},{"day":11,"title":"Drive to Kathmandu","description":"8 hour drive back to Kathmandu."}]'::jsonb,
'["Airport transfers","10 nights teahouse accommodation","Guide for 11 days","Kathmandu-Machha Khola-Kathmandu local bus","All necessary permits","11 breakfasts, 11 lunches, 11 dinners on trek"]'::jsonb,
'["Hotel in Kathmandu","Porter (optional USD 299)","Private Jeep (optional USD 320)","Hot/cold drinks","Travel insurance","Personal expenses","Tips"]'::jsonb,
'["Not open until 2008 — very remote and untouched","Visit Mu Gompa and Rachen Gompa monasteries","Milarepa''s meditation cave","Tibetan-border culture and people","Views of Mt. Manaslu (8th highest in world)","High suspension and cantilever bridges"]'::jsonb),

-- KHOPRA RIDGE TREK (Annapurna)
('Khopra Ridge Trek','khopra-ridge-trek','A hidden gem above the Annapurna region with breathtaking views from Khopra Danda and the Muldai viewpoint.','The Khopra Ridge Trek is one of the Annapurna region''s best-kept secrets. Also known as the "Khopra Danda Trek," this route takes you away from the crowded trails to a stunning ridge at 3,660m with unobstructed views of the Annapurna and Dhaulagiri ranges. The highlight is the hike to Muldai Viewpoint (3,900m) for sunrise over Dhaulagiri, Annapurna South, and Machhapuchhre. The trail passes through traditional villages, rhododendron forests, and offers a genuine off-the-beaten-path experience.','https://images.pexels.com/photos/2901209/pexels-photo-2901209.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1600','9 Days','Moderate','$780','Trek',28,
'[{"day":1,"title":"Kathmandu to Pokhara","description":"6-7 hour drive or 25 minute flight to Pokhara."},{"day":2,"title":"Pokhara to Ghandruk","description":"Drive to Ghandruk (2,012m). Explore the Gurung village."},{"day":3,"title":"Ghandruk to Tadapani","description":"5-6 hour trek through rhododendron forests to Tadapani (2,630m)."},{"day":4,"title":"Tadapani to Khopra Ridge","description":"6 hour trek through forests and pastures to Khopra Ridge (3,660m)."},{"day":5,"title":"Muldai Viewpoint Hike","description":"Early morning hike to Muldai Viewpoint (3,900m) for sunrise. Return to Khopra."},{"day":6,"title":"Khopra to Swanta","description":"5 hour descent to Swanta village."},{"day":7,"title":"Swanta to Ghorepani","description":"5 hour trek through forests to Ghorepani."},{"day":8,"title":"Poon Hill Sunrise & Trek to Nayapul","description":"Early hike to Poon Hill. Descend to Nayapul. Drive to Pokhara."},{"day":9,"title":"Pokhara to Kathmandu","description":"Drive back to Kathmandu."}]'::jsonb,
'["7 nights teahouse accommodation","1 night Pokhara hotel","Guide for 9 days","Kathmandu-Pokhara-Kathmandu tourist bus","Private car to trailhead and return","ACAP permit + TIMS card","All meals on trek"]'::jsonb,
'["Porter (optional)","Lunch/dinner in Pokhara","Hotel in Kathmandu","Hot/cold drinks","Travel insurance","Tips"]'::jsonb,
'["Muldai Viewpoint — sunrise over Dhaulagiri and Annapurna","Less crowded — true off-the-beaten-path","Panoramic Himalayan views from Khopra Ridge","Traditional Gurung villages","Rhododendron forests and alpine meadows","Combine with Poon Hill sunrise"]'::jsonb),

-- KANCHENJUNGA CIRCUIT TREK (Kanchenjunga)
('Kanchenjunga Circuit Trek','kanchenjunga-circuit-trek','An epic journey around the world''s 3rd highest mountain through remote wilderness and pristine landscapes.','The Kanchenjunga Circuit Trek is one of Nepal''s most remote and challenging treks. Circling Mt. Kanchenjunga (8,586m), the world''s 3rd highest mountain, this trek takes you through pristine wilderness, remote villages, and high alpine passes. The trail passes through the Kanchenjunga Conservation Area, home to diverse wildlife including snow leopards, Himalayan black bears, and red pandas. You''ll visit both the North and South Base Camps, cross the Sele Le Pass (4,320m), and experience the unique cultures of the Limbu, Rai, and Tibetan communities. This is a trek for those seeking true adventure and solitude.','https://images.pexels.com/photos/2387418/pexels-photo-2387418.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1600','19 Days','Challenging','$2,200','Trek',29,
'[{"day":1,"title":"Arrive in Kathmandu","description":"Arrival and hotel transfer."},{"day":2,"title":"Fly to Bhadrapur, Drive to Phidim","description":"Flight to Bhadrapur. Scenic drive to Phidim."},{"day":3,"title":"Phidim to Kande Bhanjyang","description":"Begin trekking through rice terraces and subtropical forests."},{"day":4,"title":"Kande Bhanjyang to Mamankhe","description":"Trek through Limbu and Rai villages."},{"day":5,"title":"Mamankhe to Yamphudin","description":"Enter the Kanchenjunga Conservation Area."},{"day":6,"title":"Yamphudin to Tortong","description":"Trek through dense forests with views of Kanchenjunga."},{"day":7,"title":"Tortong to Tseram","description":"Enter alpine terrain with expanding Himalayan views."},{"day":8,"title":"Tseram to Kanchenjunga South BC","description":"Visit Kanchenjunga South Base Camp (4,800m)."},{"day":9,"title":"Return to Tseram","description":"Descend back to Tseram."},{"day":10,"title":"Tseram to Ghunsa","description":"Trek through beautiful valleys to Ghunsa village."},{"day":11,"title":"Ghunsa to Khambachen","description":"Ascend through alpine meadows to Khambachen (4,050m)."},{"day":12,"title":"Khambachen to Lhonak","description":"Trek through glacial terrain to Lhonak (4,790m)."},{"day":13,"title":"Kanchenjunga North BC","description":"Day hike to Kanchenjunga North Base Camp (5,143m)."},{"day":14,"title":"Cross Sele Le Pass","description":"Cross the high Sele Le Pass (4,320m). Descend to camp."},{"day":15,"title":"Trek to Ghunsa","description":"Descend through beautiful valleys."},{"day":16,"title":"Trek to Phidim","description":"Continue descent through forests and villages."},{"day":17,"title":"Drive to Bhadrapur","description":"Scenic drive back to Bhadrapur."},{"day":18,"title":"Fly to Kathmandu","description":"Flight back to Kathmandu."},{"day":19,"title":"Departure","description":"Airport transfer."}]'::jsonb,
'["Airport transfers","Domestic flights (Kathmandu-Bhadrapur)","Hotel in Kathmandu","Teahouse/camping accommodation","All meals on trek","English-speaking guide","Porter service","Kanchenjunga Conservation Area permit","Restricted Area permit","TIMS card"]'::jsonb,
'["International flights","Nepal visa","Travel insurance","Personal gear","Hot showers","Tips","Alcoholic drinks"]'::jsonb,
'["Trek around the world''s 3rd highest mountain (8,586m)","Visit both North and South Base Camps","Cross Sele Le Pass (4,320m)","Remote wilderness — very few trekkers","Unique Limbu, Rai, and Tibetan cultures","Wildlife: snow leopards, red pandas, black bears"]'::jsonb),

-- UPPER DOLPO CIRCUIT TREK (Dolpo)
('Upper Dolpo Circuit Trek','upper-dolpo-circuit-trek','A legendary journey through ancient Buddhist landscapes, turquoise lakes, and the hidden valleys of Dolpo.','The Upper Dolpo Circuit Trek is one of the most remote and awe-inspiring treks in Nepal. Located in the far northwestern region, Dolpo is a land of ancient Tibetan Buddhist culture, arid trans-Himalayan landscapes, and stunning turquoise lakes. The trek crosses several high passes over 5,000m, including the Numa La (5,190m) and Baga La (5,070m), and visits the pristine Phoksundo Lake (3,611m) — Nepal''s deepest lake. Dolpo gained fame through Peter Matthiessen''s book "The Snow Leopard" and remains one of the most culturally and geographically unique regions of Nepal. This is a true wilderness expedition requiring camping.','https://images.pexels.com/photos/417173/pexels-photo-417173.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1600','24 Days','Challenging','$3,200','Trek',30,
'[{"day":1,"title":"Arrive in Kathmandu","description":"Arrival and expedition briefing."},{"day":2,"title":"Fly to Nepalgunj","description":"Domestic flight to Nepalgunj."},{"day":3,"title":"Fly to Juphal, Trek to Chhepka","description":"Flight to Juphal. Begin trekking through pine forests."},{"day":4,"title":"Chhepka to Phoksundo Lake","description":"Trek to the stunning turquoise Phoksundo Lake (3,611m)."},{"day":5,"title":"Explore Phoksundo","description":"Day hike to the Ringmo village and Phoksundo waterfall."},{"day":6,"title":"Phoksundo to Thasher Manla","description":"Begin crossing the first high passes."},{"day":7,"title":"Cross Numa La Pass","description":"Cross Numa La (5,190m). Camp on the far side."},{"day":8,"title":"Cross Baga La Pass","description":"Cross Baga La (5,070m). Descend to the Shey Valley."},{"day":9,"title":"Shey Gompa","description":"Visit the ancient Shey Gompa monastery."},{"day":10,"title":"Shey Gompa to Namdune","description":"Trek through the pristine Shey Valley."},{"day":11,"title":"Namdune to Saldang","description":"Enter the main Dolpo settlement area."},{"day":12,"title":"Explore Saldang","description":"Rest day exploring the largest village in Dolpo."},{"day":13,"title":"Saldang to Yangtse Gompa","description":"Visit the remote Yangtse Gompa."},{"day":14,"title":"Yangtse to Sibu","description":"Continue through the trans-Himalayan landscape."},{"day":15,"title":"Sibu to Jeng La Phedi","description":"Approach the Jeng La Pass."},{"day":16,"title":"Cross Jeng La Pass","description":"Cross Jeng La (5,110m). Descend to Tokyu."},{"day":17,"title":"Tokyu to Taling","description":"Descend through juniper forests."},{"day":18,"title":"Taling to Dunai","description":"Return to the main trailhead."},{"day":19,"title":"Dunai to Juphal","description":"Final day of trekking."},{"day":20,"title":"Fly to Kathmandu","description":"Flight via Nepalgunj to Kathmandu."}]'::jsonb,
'["All domestic flights","All camping equipment (tents, mattresses, kitchen)","Full board meals on trek","English-speaking guide","Cook and kitchen staff","Camping permits and National Park fees","TIMS card","Satellite phone","Emergency first aid kit"]'::jsonb,
'["International flights","Nepal visa","Travel insurance","Personal clothing and sleeping bag","Tips","Alcoholic drinks","Hot showers (not available)"]'::jsonb,
'["Phoksundo Lake — Nepal''s deepest and most beautiful lake","Cross three high passes over 5,000m","Ancient Tibetan Buddhist monasteries","Remote wilderness — see The Snow Leopard country","Unique Dolpo-pa culture","Camping expedition — true adventure"]'::jsonb),

-- MAKALU BASE CAMP TREK (Makalu)
('Makalu Base Camp Trek','makalu-base-camp-trek','A remote wilderness trek to the base of the world''s 5th highest mountain through pristine forests and alpine meadows.','The Makalu Base Camp Trek is one of Nepal''s most challenging and rewarding treks. The trail leads to the base of Mt. Makalu (8,463m), the world''s 5th highest mountain, through some of the most pristine and biodiverse forests in Nepal. The trek passes through the Makalu-Barun National Park, which features a spectacular altitude gradient from subtropical forests at 400m to alpine terrain above 5,000m. The region is home to over 3,000 species of flowering plants, 440 species of birds, and 75 species of mammals including the elusive snow leopard. The trek crosses the Shipton La Pass (4,217m) and offers incredible views of Makalu, Everest, Lhotse, and Chamlang.','https://images.pexels.com/photos/2387418/pexels-photo-2387418.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1600','19 Days','Challenging','$2,100','Trek',31,
'[{"day":1,"title":"Arrive in Kathmandu","description":"Arrival and expedition briefing."},{"day":2,"title":"Fly to Tumlingtar","description":"Scenic flight to Tumlingtar. Prepare for trek."},{"day":3,"title":"Trek to Num","description":"Begin trekking through subtropical forests and rice terraces."},{"day":4,"title":"Num to Seduwa","description":"Ascend through the Arun Valley."},{"day":5,"title":"Seduwa to Tashigaon","description":"Enter Makalu-Barun National Park."},{"day":6,"title":"Tashigaon to Khongma","description":"Trek through rhododendron and bamboo forests."},{"day":7,"title":"Khongma to Mumbuk","description":"Enter alpine terrain above the treeline."},{"day":8,"title":"Mumbuk to Nehe Kharka","description":"Cross the Shipton La Pass (4,217m)."},{"day":9,"title":"Nehe Kharka to Base Camp","description":"Arrive at Makalu Base Camp (4,870m)."},{"day":10,"title":"Explore Makalu BC","description":"Day exploring the base camp area. Views of Makalu."},{"day":11,"title":"Begin descent","description":"Start the return journey."},{"day":12,"title":"Retrace to Khongma","description":"Descend through alpine terrain."},{"day":13,"title":"Khongma to Tashigaon","description":"Continue descending through forests."},{"day":14,"title":"Tashigaon to Num","description":"Return through the Arun Valley."},{"day":15,"title":"Num to Tumlingtar","description":"Final day of trekking."},{"day":16,"title":"Fly to Kathmandu","description":"Return flight."}]'::jsonb,
'["Airport transfers","Domestic flights","Hotel in Kathmandu","Teahouse/camping accommodation","All meals on trek","English-speaking guide","Porter service","Makalu-Barun National Park permit","TIMS card","Satellite phone"]'::jsonb,
'["International flights","Nepal visa","Travel insurance","Personal gear","Tips","Alcoholic drinks"]'::jsonb,
'["Trek to the base of the world''s 5th highest mountain (8,463m)","Cross Shipton La Pass (4,217m)","Makalu-Barun National Park — incredible biodiversity","Remote wilderness — very few trekkers","Views of Makalu, Everest, Lhotse, and Chamlang","Spectacular altitude gradient from 400m to 5,000m+"]'::jsonb),

